  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday) \nIssued at 129 AM MDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nOn Thursday, the high centers up over AZ with heights only dropping \nby a decameter or two. This placement will continue to allow drier \nair to spill into NM from the northwest, and PWATs are projected to \nfall to 0.5 inch in many northwestern zones with an increasing \ngradient toward the southeastern zones where readings would hold \naround 1.2 to 1.3 inches. This drying and the washing out of the \nprevious day's surface boundary will really limit storms over much \nof the northern half of the forecast area with cells most likely to \ninitiate in the Gila and Sacramentos while struggling to move far \noff of the high terrain. High temperatures would keep gaining a \ncouple of degrees in western zones on Thursday, pushing them 5 to 10 \ndegrees above climatology.\n\nHigh pressure will not move much on Friday, holding near or to the \nsouthwest of NM, and the drier westerly flow will continue to filter \nsoutheastward over many zones. PWATs would fall to around 0.5 to 0.8 \ninch for most zones, the exception being the far southern and \nwestern tier of the forecast area where moisture would hold or even \nbegin to pivot back in (far west). This will put the kibosh on \nstorms over much of the forecast area while rebounding temperatures \nexpand eastward, climbing 5 to almost 15 degrees above normal.\n\nHigh pressure looks to slide eastward along the southern border of \nNM into Saturday before moving into central TX on Sunday. As this \noccurs, another deep low will enter the northwestern states, setting \nup a more moist west southwest flow into NM, as deep subtropical \nmoisture will be staging over the Gulf of CA. The moisture will be \nheavily modified and subdued by the time it returns to NM, but it \nwould sufficiently reintroduce storm chances over the high terrain \nthis weekend. The northwest states low will be racing into the \nnorthern Great Plains by Monday, but essentially the same trend \nlooks to hold for NM with a faint plume of monsoon moisture \nstretching from the Sonoran and Chihuahuan deserts northeastward \ninto our northern mountains. Temperatures would reduce a couple to a \nfew degrees each day this weekend into Monday with western zones \nfalling close to average while departures in eastern zones undergo \nshrinking departures from normal.",
